%S A399786 2,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,26,288,583,3041,6835,53208,195205,1231813,4334124,
%T A399786 14750107,43274540,65701065,136162628,158813028,233415984
%N A399786 Power chains: Number of essentially different permutations of the numbers 1 to n such that the sum of any two consecutive numbers is a perfect power, with each circular permutation counted n times.
%C A399786 This sequence counts all essentially different power chains with reversals not counted as different: the linear (non-circular) chains counted by A399783, together with the power loops in A399784, each counted n times (see Example section). Linear chains in row first occur for n = 7, while power loops first occur for n = 17.
%C A399786 Note that A399785 counts each circular solution only once.
%C A399786 This sequence, together with A399783, A399784 and A399785, gives the four possible distinct counts of power chains (see Crossrefs).
%C A399786 In terms of graph theory, these numbers count Hamiltonian paths that cannot be closed to form a Hamiltonian cycle, together with Hamiltonian cycles, with reversals not counted as distinct, and with each circular solution counted n times.
%H A399786 Diophante, <a href="http://www.diophante.fr/problemes-par-themes/h-graphes-et-circuits/681-h103-les-chaines-de-puissances">H103. Les chaînes de puissances</a> (in French).
%F A399786 a(n) = A399783(n) + n*A399784(n).
%F A399786 a(n) = A399785(n) + (n-1)*A399784(n).
%e A399786 a(17) = 288, since there are A399783(17) = 237 linear permutations, together with A399784(17) = 3 circular loops, each counted 17 times; thus 237 + 3*17 = 288.
%e A399786 For example, the loop [1-8-17-10-6-2-7-9-16-11-14-13-3-5-4-12-15] gives 17 distinct linear chains by choosing each of its 17 elements in turn as the first element, for example [8-17-10-6-2-7-9-16-11-14-13-3-5-4-12-15-1], [17-10-6-2-7-9-16-11-14-13-3-5-4-12-15-1-8], ... The closing condition is satisfied because 15 + 1 = 16 = 2^4.
%Y A399786 The four possible distinct counts of power chains: A399783 (number of linear permutations), A399784 (number of circular permutations), A399785 (number of total permutations counting each circular solution only once), this sequence (number of total permutations counting each circular solution n times).
%Y A399786 Cf. A001597 (perfect powers), A071983 (similar, but for square chains).
%K A399786 nonn,more,new
%O A399786 7,1
